# Keep the language bar describing what the project is written in. GitHub counts
# every tracked file by extension, and a Chinese-titled Markdown file came out as
# an unrecognised entry in the bar, which says nothing useful about the code.
#
# Documentation is not a language, so it is excluded from the statistics rather
# than allowed to compete with the source.
*.md linguist-documentation
*.txt linguist-documentation

# Line-ending behaviour, kept explicit so a checkout on this machine and a CI
# checkout on a Windows runner produce the same bytes. The PowerShell scripts are
# read by Windows PowerShell 5.1, which needs a BOM to read them as UTF-8;
# rewriting them with a plain LF would silently break the Chinese strings they
# contain, so they keep CRLF and no encoding override is declared.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cpp text eol=crlf
*.hpp text eol=crlf
*.in text eol=crlf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
